# daisyUI component catalog

`references/theming-and-components.md` covers the handful of components
this project's own templates actually use (`card`, `btn`, `input`,
`checkbox`). This file is the wider map — daisyUI ships **80+**
components, and reaching for one of them beats hand-composing the same
look from raw Tailwind utilities almost every time. Adapted from
daisyUI's own [official skill](https://daisyui.com/docs/skill/) into
this project's shape.

## Discovery protocol — before writing a single utility class

1. Name the actual UI element/behavior you need (not just a rough
   description) — "a dismissible message strip" is an `alert`, "a
   floating action trigger" is a `fab`.
2. Scan the category list below for a plausible match.
3. Check that component's exact classes at
   [daisyui.com/components](https://daisyui.com/components/) — part
   names, modifiers, and required markup structure vary per component
   and are worth confirming rather than guessing.
4. Only fall back to raw Tailwind utilities once you've confirmed no
   component fits — a `card`/`btn`/`alert`/`modal`-shaped need almost
   always has a matching component already.

## Component categories

| Category | Components |
|---|---|
| Navigation & layout | navbar, drawer, dock, menu, breadcrumbs, pagination, steps, timeline |
| Forms & input | input, select, checkbox, radio, toggle, textarea, file-input, range, rating, otp |
| Feedback | alert, badge, progress, loading, toast, tooltip, modal |
| Content display | card, table, carousel, avatar, chat, diff, divider, list, stat |
| Interactive | button, dropdown, collapse, accordion, tabs, swap, fab |
| Specialized | hero, footer, calendar, countdown, skeleton, status, validator, kbd |
| Visual effects | aura, mask, hover-3d, hover-gallery, text-rotate, stack |
| Mockups | browser, code, phone, window |

## Usage rules

- Apply component classes directly to elements (`class="btn"`, `class="card"`) — no extra wrapper markup required beyond what each component's docs show.
- Combine **component + part + style + behavior** classes as needed, e.g. `btn btn-primary btn-outline btn-sm` (component: `btn`; style: `btn-primary`/`btn-outline`; size/behavior: `btn-sm`) — daisyUI classes are designed to stack, not to be chosen one-at-a-time.
- Reach for the semantic color tokens (`primary`, `base-200`, `error`, ...) documented in `references/theming-and-components.md` rather than hardcoded Tailwind colors like `text-gray-800` — hardcoded colors don't adapt when the active theme changes, silently breaking dark mode or any custom theme added later.
- Use plain Tailwind utilities for anything a daisyUI component doesn't cover (spacing, one-off layout tweaks) — daisyUI classes and Tailwind utilities are meant to be mixed on the same element, not treated as separate systems.
- Avoid `!` (important) modifiers unless resolving a genuine specificity conflict — reaching for `!` habitually usually means the wrong daisyUI modifier was picked, not that Tailwind needs overriding.
- Use responsive prefixes (`md:`, `lg:`, ...) for flexbox/grid layout changes across breakpoints, same as anywhere else in Tailwind — daisyUI components don't have their own separate responsive system.

## Component-specific gotchas worth knowing before you reach for these

- **Accordion**: radio inputs used to drive an accordion's open/close state must share the same `name` attribute across the group, or only the first one will ever behave like part of a group.
- **Drawer**: the toggle `<input>` needs a unique `id`, and its `<label>` must reference that same `id` — a copy-pasted drawer with a stale `id`/`for` pair silently stops toggling.
- **Modal**: prefer the native HTML `<dialog>` element (`daisyui.com/components/modal`) over the older div-based modal pattern where possible — it gets focus-trapping and Escape-to-close for free from the browser.
- **hover-3d**: requires exactly nine children (one real content element plus eight invisible hover zones) — adding or removing a child breaks the effect rather than degrading gracefully.
- **text-rotate**: limited to a maximum of six lines per rotation cycle.

For exact per-component markup, part names, and every modifier, check the live docs at [daisyui.com/components](https://daisyui.com/components/) — this file is a map for deciding *which* component to reach for, not a substitute for its actual class reference.
